flowchart TD
  START[Request arrives] --> AUTH{HMAC valid and fresh?}
  AUTH -- No --> R401[401; audit rejection; no body persistence]
  AUTH -- Yes --> SCHEMA{Allowlisted schema and scrubber pass?}
  SCHEMA -- No --> R422[422/500; audit rejection; no mutation]
  SCHEMA -- Yes --> GATE{Mutation gate OPEN?}
  GATE -- No/Unknown --> R503[503; fail closed; page owner]
  GATE -- Yes --> DONE{Completed idempotency record?}
  DONE -- Yes --> DUP[200 duplicate; no Jira call]
  DONE -- No --> LOCK{Atomic lock acquired?}
  LOCK -- No --> BUSY[503 or bounded retry; no Jira call]
  LOCK -- Yes --> OUTBOX[Durably accept bounded work]
  OUTBOX --> JIRA{Jira outcome known?}
  JIRA -- Success --> AUD[Audit mutation + completion record]
  JIRA -- Retryable failure --> RETRY[Bounded retry with backoff]
  JIRA -- Timeout/unknown --> RECON[Pause gate; reconcile by external key]
  RETRY --> JIRA
  RECON --> AUD
  AUD --> OK[Release lock conditionally; 200 only after safe acceptance]

%% Safety notes:
%% - All identifiers in probes are synthetic.
%% - No secret values or raw webhook bodies belong in logs or evidence.
%% - The gate must default to PAUSED when control state cannot be established.
%% - No path performs publication, deletion, restoration, or automatic Jira closure.
